</section>

<section class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="h4">Key Characters</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Simon Jarrett</strong> - the protagonist, a man with brain damage from a car accident who undergoes an experimental brain scan.</li>
        <li><strong>Catherine Chung</strong> - a scan of a PATHOS-II researcher, stored in a device that Simon carries with him.</li>
        <li><strong>The WAU</strong> - the station's AI, which spreads through the facility and its machines and warps the people it was meant to preserve.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="h4">Reception and Legacy</h2>
    <p>
        SOMA was praised by critics and players for its story and atmosphere. It is often cited as one
        of the best narrative horror games, and it was later given a "Safe Mode" option that
        lets players explore the story without being hunted by monsters.
    </p>
</section>
